{
  "game_concepts": [
    {
      "id": "production_mastery",
      "name": "Production mastery of goods",
      "icon": "production_bonus.png",
      "description": "The city can increase the professional level of its workers in producing goods.\n\n
        • Production mastery is tracked separately for each good:\n
        • A thousand units of brandy do not earn a rank for rum. Every good has its own counter.\n
        • Only units released by recipes of city buildings are counted. Goods bought from towns and raw 
        material gathered on the map are not.\n
        • The first rank comes at 1000 units of the good, the second at 3000 in total, that is 2000 
        more on top of the first thousand.\n
        • Each rank adds one quality level to all future output of that good in every city building.\n
        • The scale ends at level 4: a perfect good is not improved further. Mastery does not change the 
        quality of the raw material or the goods already in storage.\n
        • A good made with an additional ingredient is counted to its base good; the dye or the spice 
        gets no rank of its own.\n
        • The Effects tab shows one row per mastered good. A building name carries one star when the 
        building makes any mastered good; the exact ranks are in the building tooltip. A new rank is 
        reported as an important message and kept in the journal."
    }
  ]
}
